# Infrastructure

## Principles

**Terraform shapes environments; scripts ship artifacts.** Don’t conflate `terraform apply` with day-to-day image push unless the task explicitly ties them.

**Base-server changes are high risk.** Diffs touching laed-base need human review before apply (`DECISIONS.md`).

**Networking facts must match reality.** Private vs public route metrics and security-group source CIDRs are about which NIC replies—wrong values fail silently as timeouts, not obvious errors. Read examples in-repo before editing.

**GPU data ownership** follows the daemon user on the instance—permissions are operational correctness, not polish.

**Runtime apps don’t call Ollama directly.** GPU hosts serve models; LAED talks to LiteLLM on the backbone network.

Billing alerts may be manual console work where no Terraform resource exists—document, don’t invent resources.
